    "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\n\n## Overview\n\nMatch the Python DeepSeek V4.1 encoder to the updated reference [`encoding/`](https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017/tree/main/encoding). Rust counterpart: #62200.\n\nAffects both V4.1-Flash checkpoints (launch and 1017). DeepSeek fixed the turn handling in both repos ([launch `314113f`](https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash/commit/314113f8a7dadb388215396ba5fbee2c610a04d6), 1017 release); their `encoding/` is now identical. The image-token check has been in the reference since launch.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Tool results alone no longer start a new user turn, so reasoning before a tool call is kept.\n- Literal `<\uff5cdeepseek_image\uff5c>` in message text or reasoning returns 400.\n- All five reference golden prompts match. V4 is unchanged.\n\n## Examples\n\n**1. Tool call in thinking mode, with no `tools` field in the request**\n\n```python\n[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"What's the weather in Paris? Answer in Fahrenheit.\"},\n {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"\", \"reasoning\": \"Tool returns Celsius; convert to Fahrenheit.\",\n  \"tool_calls\": [{\"id\": \"c1\", \"type\": \"function\", \"function\": {\"name\": \"get_weather\", \"arguments\": \"{\\\"city\\\": \\\"Paris\\\"}\"}}]},\n {\"role\": \"tool\", \"tool_call_id\": \"c1\", \"content\": \"{\\\"temp_c\\\": 20}\"}]\n```\n\nBefore (reasoning dropped):\n```\n<\uff5cUser\uff5c>What's the weather in Paris? Answer in Fahrenheit.<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c></think>\n\n<\uff5cDSML\uff5c calls>...\n```\nAfter (reasoning kept, same as the reference encoder):\n```\n<\uff5cUser\uff5c>What's the weather in Paris? Answer in Fahrenheit.<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c><think>Tool returns Celsius; convert to Fahrenheit.</think>\n\n<\uff5cDSML\uff5c calls>...\n```\n\n**2. Literal image token in text**\n\n```python\n[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"hi <\uff5cdeepseek_image\uff5c>\"}]\n```\n\nBefore: accepted, so the prompt has an image placeholder with no image. After: 400.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pytest tests/tokenizers_/test_deepseek_v41.py tests/tokenizers_/test_deepseek_v4.py`: 84 passed. The new tests fail on main.\n- E2E on 8x H100 (TP8, recipe H100 flags, DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017): the prompt keeps the tool-call reasoning and matches the reference encoder; the literal image token returns 400.\n- GSM8K (chat, thinking off, 1319 questions): 0.970.\n\n## Details\n\nNot a duplicate: #60792 (image order) and other open V4.1 tokenizer PRs don't change turn boundaries or placeholder validation. Fixtures are copied from the 1017 repo (MIT).\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
